\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\sa240\itap0{\f0\fs24\lang1033{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch For a number p and its digit reversal reverse(p) to both be expressible as 2n\'b2 + 2n + 1, both must satisfy the last-two-digit constraints. This creates a symmetry:}{\f0\fs24\lang1033{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\sa240\itap0{\f0\fs24\lang1033{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch If p ends in digits 'ab', then reverse(p) starts with digits 'ba'. For both to be valid candidates:}{\f0\fs24\lang1033{\*\listtag0}\par}
{\listtext\pard\fi-360\li720\bullet 	}\pard\plain{\ltrpar\ql\fi-360\li720\s30{\*\abilist\abilistid11200\abilistparentid0\abilistlevel1\abistartat1{\abifieldfont NULL}{\abilistdecimal .}{\abilistdelim %L.}{\abiliststyle None}}{\*\pn\pnql\pnstart1\pnlvlblt{\pntxtb\bullet}}\ls1\ilvl0\itap0{\s30\f0\fs24\lang1033{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch p must end in one of: 01, 13, 21, 41, 61, 81}{\s30\f0\fs24\lang1033{\*\listtag0}\par}
